plaso.tsv: what plaso (the log2timeline/plaso:20260720 Docker image) reads
from the logs in tests/fixtures/plaso/ with its text/apache_access,
text/confluence_access, text/jira_access and text/bitbucket_access parsers
(psort -o json_line), one line per event: the file, the time (microseconds
since 1970, UTC; Bitbucket's local times as plaso keeps them, as if UTC),
then the values compared, by parser:

- apache_access: address, user, request, status, bytes, referer, user agent,
  virtual host, port;
- confluence and jira: address, user, method, path, protocol, status, bytes,
  referer, user agent, duration (ms), thread, forwarded-for;
- bitbucket: address, user, method, path, protocol, user agent, status,
  bytes read, bytes written, duration (ms), protocol, request id, labels,
  session, SSH repository, mesh execution id.

`-` is written as empty: both read it as no value. Written from plaso's
output, not from this crate.

cloud.tsv: what plaso reads from aws_elb_access.log and
azure_application_gateway_access.json (uncompressed) with its
text/aws_elb_access parser and jsonl/azure_application_gateway_access_log
plugin, written by plaso.py from psort's JSON lines; one line per event:
the file, the time (ISO 8601; the network load balancer's local times as
if UTC), plaso's name for it, the parser, and every value plaso read, as
name=value (see plaso.py). Made on a Debian host with Docker, the two logs
in /tmp/oracle/in, from the crate root:

  sudo docker run --rm -v /tmp/oracle:/data log2timeline/plaso:20260720 \
    log2timeline --status_view none -q \
    --parsers 'text/aws_elb_access,jsonl/azure_application_gateway_access_log' \
    --storage-file /data/out.plaso /data/in
  sudo docker run --rm -v /tmp/oracle:/data log2timeline/plaso:20260720 \
    psort --status_view none -q -a -o json_line -w /data/out.jsonl /data/out.plaso
  python3 -I tests/oracle/plaso.py /tmp/oracle/out.jsonl > tests/oracle/cloud.tsv

(psort's -a keeps events it would drop as duplicates; none here.)

atlassian.tsv: what plaso reads from atlassian-bitbucket.log,
atlassian-bitbucket-audit.log, atlassian-confluence.log and
atlassian-jira.log (tests/fixtures/plaso/atlassian/, uncompressed) with
its text/atlassian_bitbucket, text/bitbucket_audit,
text/atlassian_confluence and text/atlassian_jira plugins, in cloud.tsv's
form (written by plaso.py). The Bitbucket plugins and the Jira and
Confluence ones are run apart: with all four enabled, plaso's
text/atlassian_bitbucket claims Jira's and Confluence's samples too (its
guard against their bracketed logger doesn't hold), leaving
"] method" at the start of each message. Jira's and Confluence's plugins
are the same grammar, so plaso reads both samples with the first,
text/atlassian_confluence. Made on a Debian host with Docker, the
Bitbucket logs in /tmp/oracle/a/in, Jira's and Confluence's in
/tmp/oracle/b/in, from the crate root:

  sudo docker run --rm -v /tmp/oracle/a:/data log2timeline/plaso:20260720 \
    log2timeline --status_view none -q \
    --parsers 'text/atlassian_bitbucket,text/bitbucket_audit' \
    --storage-file /data/out.plaso /data/in
  sudo docker run --rm -v /tmp/oracle/a:/data log2timeline/plaso:20260720 \
    psort --status_view none -q -a -o json_line -w /data/out.jsonl /data/out.plaso
  sudo docker run --rm -v /tmp/oracle/b:/data log2timeline/plaso:20260720 \
    log2timeline --status_view none -q \
    --parsers 'text/atlassian_confluence,text/atlassian_jira' \
    --storage-file /data/out.plaso /data/in
  sudo docker run --rm -v /tmp/oracle/b:/data log2timeline/plaso:20260720 \
    psort --status_view none -q -a -o json_line -w /data/out.jsonl /data/out.plaso
  cat /tmp/oracle/a/out.jsonl /tmp/oracle/b/out.jsonl > /tmp/oracle/ab.jsonl
  python3 -I tests/oracle/plaso.py /tmp/oracle/ab.jsonl > tests/oracle/atlassian.tsv

plaso has no sample of Jira's own layout (its Jira sample is in
Confluence's) nor of the audit log file Jira, Confluence and Bitbucket
Data Center write (and no parser for it): those are checked on the
synthetic logs of tests/fixtures/synthetic/ (made by its gen.py), not
against plaso: unverified.
